{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/10286","id":2817012390,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLCAjRs6n6DKm","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/10286","diff_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/10286.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/10286.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/10286","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/10286/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/10286/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/10286/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/statuses/556659aafc68f184c545e05d9b5d09947293b62a","number":10286,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[2/4] Introduce Chunked-SGMV kernels and corresponding LoRA backend for improved performance","user":{"login":"lifuhuang","id":3427331,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjczMzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3427331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang","html_url":"https://github.com/lifuhuang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lifuhuang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"(Huge thanks to @Fridge003 for the extremely valuable discussions and insights)\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe current LoRA solution has been suffering from disproportionate performance degradation compared with base model as batch size grows. For example, when benchmarking the current implementation, the median e2e latency with LoRA is appx 2x larger than the base model at request rate 4 and 3x larger at request rate 8.\r\n\r\nDuring investigation, we found out that the current LoRA kernels and the previously deprecated flashinfer kernels are both dividing computations by batch size (e.g., grid dim = `[max_seq_len * cdiv(k_dim, BLOCK_K) , batch size]`), which suffers from the following problems:\r\n1. **Prefill**: prefill batches with high variance in sequence length causes very high max_seq_len, therefore lots of no-op CTAs are launched, wasting GPU resources. \r\n2. **Decode**:  as all sequence in a batch have lengths 1, effectively 15/16 of each CTA's compute power is wasted (because 16 is the smallest M for tensor cores).\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nTo overcome this issues, a new solution (Chunked SGMV) is introduced, based on Punica-style gather + chunking: \r\n- Step 1 - Gather: group all input tokens by LoRA weight to facilitate batching. This is identical to the SGMV solution in Punica.\r\n- Step 2 - Chunking: splitting the tokens into constant-sized chunks (e.g., 16) at LoRA batch preprocessing phase to reduce fragmentation & launched CTA numbers when token distribution across groups are highly skewed.\r\n\r\nWith this approach, we observed significant perf improvement across the board.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\r\n\r\nBenchmark command: \r\n```\r\npython -m sglang.launch_server \\\r\n    --model-path meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct \\\r\n    --disable-radix-cache \\\r\n    --lora-paths lora=algoprog/fact-generation-llama-3.1-8b-instruct-lora \\\r\n    --lora-backend csgmv \\\r\n    --port 30000\r\npython3 -m sglang.bench_serving --backend sglang  --num-prompt 1000 --request-rate <2,8,16,inf>  --dataset-name sharegpt --lora-name lora \r\n```\r\n<table>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><img width=\"1180\" height=\"780\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4fa98da5-af78-461d-8775-582b3d971752\" /></td>\r\n<td><img width=\"1180\" height=\"780\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/055a7bfb-50a1-434f-a187-05989041d782\" /></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><img width=\"1180\" height=\"780\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e11d1c0-a55d-472b-9d20-bc0c199392b4\" /></td>\r\n<td><img width=\"1180\" height=\"780\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3688738-f2b7-4289-913d-897b4d15156a\" /></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n### Median E2E Latency (ms)\r\n| Request Rate | 2 | 8 | 16 | inf |\r\n|--------------|------|------|-------|-------|\r\n| Baseline | 1156 | 2424 | 8002 | 51212 |\r\n| CSGMV | 1050 (**-9%**) | 1452 (**-40%**) | 2382 (**-70%**) | 9905 (**-81%**) |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Median ITL (ms)\r\n| Request Rate | 2 | 8 | 16 | inf |\r\n|--------------|------|------|------|------|\r\n| Baseline | 10.1 | 18.5 | 59.7 | 118.2 |\r\n| CSGMV | 8.9 (**-12%**) | 9.73 (**-47%**) | 12.3 (**-79%**) | 36.4 (**-69%**) |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Median TTFT (ms)\r\n| Request Rate | 2 | 8 | 16 | inf |\r\n|--------------|------|------|------|-------|\r\n| Baseline | 47 | 55 | 98 | 15157 |\r\n| CSGMV | 47 (**0%**) | 50 (**-9%**) | 75 (**-23%**) | 3128 (**-79%**) |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Total Throughput (tokens/s)\r\n| Request Rate | 2 | 8 | 16 | inf |\r\n|--------------|------|------|------|------|\r\n| Baseline | 942 | 3557 | 5286 | 4930 |\r\n| CSGMV | 942 (**0%**) | 3665 (**+3%**) | 6582 (**+25%**) | 8005 (**+62%**) |\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n* testing with phi4mm shows normal output:\r\n<img width=\"490\" height=\"708\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3a81b871-778d-4f99-9718-933724871f59\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-09-10T22:29:50Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T03:44:04Z","closed_at":"2025-09-15T23:04:04Z","merged_at":"2025-09-15T23:04:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"3f41b48c4079d0adaf17ce7adf308c6a0d947ad0","assignee":{"login":"Fridge003","id":56809903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2ODA5OTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56809903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003","html_url":"https://github.com/Fridge003","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fridge003/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"assignees":[{